course: dictionary
lesson: 12606
title: Discouragement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Discouragement is a noun. It is the feeling you get when you lose confidence or hope, so you do not want to try any more. «After she lost the spelling bee, Priya felt a heavy discouragement and wanted to stop practising.» The clues are lost, heavy and wanted to stop, so discouragement must mean losing hope.
explain: Discouragement can also mean something that makes people less likely to do something. «A big fine is a discouragement to dropping litter.» A fine does not feel sad. It is a thing that puts people off, so they think twice before they litter.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Priya felt a heavy ___ and wanted to stop.» Lost hope fits well, so you have found the right meaning. If the sentence still makes sense with your meaning, you are probably right.
fact: Discouragement means a feeling of having lost confidence or hope.
fact: Discouragement can also mean something that makes people less likely to do something, as in «a discouragement to dropping litter».
fact: «Despite discouragement» means carrying on even though things are hard.
fact: Heroes in stories often face discouragement, but they keep going.
fact: Teachers and coaches can help pupils overcome discouragement after a failed test or a lost match.
exercise: «After failing the test three times, Ravi felt a deep discouragement.» What does discouragement mean here? | *A loss of hope, so you do not want to try any more | Great excitement about the next test | A loud noise in the hall | A new pair of shoes
exercise: «A big fine is a discouragement to dropping litter.» What does discouragement mean in this sentence? | *Something that makes people less likely to do it | A prize for the tidiest street | A kind of soup | Something that makes people run faster
exercise: «Despite discouragement from his friends, Sam kept practising the violin.» What did Sam do? | Sam was in a great hurry to go home | Sam forgot where he had put his violin | Sam stopped practising at once | *Sam kept going even though things were hard
test: «Maya wanted to quit after the match, but her coach helped her beat the ___.» | Hunger | Sleepiness | Excitement | *Discouragement
test: «A rule about bikes is a ___ to riding on the pavement, so fewer children do it.» | *Discouragement | Prize | Surprise | Invitation
exam: «Heroes in the story faced discouragement but kept going. Which meaning fits best?» | A sudden surprise party | *Loss of hope or confidence | A type of storm | Shout of joy
